msgid "9. Detection capability"
msgstr ""

#: ../../examples/notebooks/09_detection_capability.ipynb:10004
msgid "Can we detect a companion 10⁴ times fainter than its star, 6 λ/D away, behind a vortex coronagraph? This notebook answers with the tools of a detection study (use case UC7):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../examples/notebooks/09_detection_capability.ipynb:10007
msgid "a **matched filter** (the Neyman-Pearson test of a known signal) applied to many noisy exposures, with and without the companion;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../examples/notebooks/09_detection_capability.ipynb:10009
#, python-brace-format
msgid "the empirical **ROC curve**, compared with its analytic form $P_D = Q(Q^{-1}(P_{FA}) - d)$;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../examples/notebooks/09_detection_capability.ipynb:10010
msgid "the **contrast curve** of a residual image (5σ, with the small-sample penalty of Mawet et al. 2014);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../examples/notebooks/09_detection_capability.ipynb:10011
msgid "the **detection capability** versus separation and contrast."
msgstr ""

